  "text": "The drawbacks next: whole seeds can pass through partly undigested. Human research found much better lignan availability after crushing or milling, so grinding matters if you want more than the fibre. A sudden fibre jump can upset digestion. Large amounts can bring bloating, fullness, or diarrhoea, so it makes sense to build up gradually. Normal servings are much smaller than 100 grams. A spoonful is useful, but it delivers only a fraction of this stat sheet in a real meal.",
